<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nalikwanda</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nalikwanda is the royal barge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/litunga">Litunga</a>, the king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lozi-people">Lozi</a> of Barotseland in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a>. Painted in black and white stripes and topped by a model elephant, it is paddled by about a hundred men during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuomboka">Kuomboka</a> ceremony, when the Litunga moves from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lealui">Lealui</a> on the floodplain to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limulunga">Limulunga</a> on higher ground as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambezi">Zambezi</a> floods.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nalikwanda.jpg" alt="Nalikwanda" width="320" height="371" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FXXX · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Zambia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
